{"name":"Harvest Time","hex":"#cf875f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"harvest time","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time of year during which harvest occurs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harvest_time"}],"entries":[{"title":"Harvest Time (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Harvest Time is a 2004 Russian drama film directed by Marina Razbezhkina. It was entered into the 26th Moscow International Film Festival."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4f/Harvest_Time_2004_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvest_Time_(film)","wikidata":"Q15710747"},{"title":"Harvest Time (Elonkorjuu album)","blocks":[{"text":"Harvest Time is the debut album from Finnish progressive rock band Elonkorjuu, originally released in 1972. It was re-issued as a CD formation in 2002. The album is inspired by groups like Cream and Free with more progressive style."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/09/Elonkorjuu_Harvest_Time.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvest_Time_(Elonkorjuu_album)","wikidata":"Q17134045"},{"title":"Harvest Time (Mowers)","blocks":[{"text":"Harvest Time (Mowers) (Russian: Страдная пора (Косцы)) is a painting by Russian artist Grigoriy Myasoedov (1834–1911), completed in 1887. It is kept in the State Russian Museum in St. Petersburg (Inventory Zh-6899). The size is 164 × 282 cm (according to other data, 179 × 275 cm). The work, combining elements of domestic genre and landscape, is devoted to the theme of peasant labor during the harvest. The painting was originally known under the title Harvest Time; later, the names Harvest and Croppers were also used. Modern literature usually uses the double title, Harvest Time (Mowers) or Harvest Time. Mowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Grigorij_Grigorjewitsch_Mjassojedow_003.jpg/330px-Grigorij_Grigorjewitsch_Mjassojedow_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvest_Time_(Mowers)","wikidata":"Q56309559"},{"title":"Harvest","blocks":[{"text":"Harvesting is the process of collecting plants, animals, or fish as food, especially the process of gathering mature crops, and \"the harvest\" also refers to the collected crops. Reaping is the cutting of grain or pulses for harvest, typically using a scythe, sickle, or reaper. On smaller farms with minimal mechanization, harvesting is the most labor-intensive activity of the growing season. On large mechanized farms, harvesting uses farm machinery, such as the combine harvester. Automation has increased the efficiency of both the seeding and harvesting processes. Specialized harvesting equipment, using conveyor belts for gentle gripping and mass transport, replaces the manual task of removing each seedling by hand. The term \"harvesting\" in general usage may include immediate postharvest handling, including cleaning, sorting, packing, and cooling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Agriculture_in_Volgograd_Oblast_002.JPG/330px-Agriculture_in_Volgograd_Oblast_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvest","wikidata":"Q213753"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Myasoyedov_by_Repin.jpg/500px-Myasoyedov_by_Repin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Myasoyedov_by_Repin.jpg/500px-Myasoyedov_by_Repin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ilya Repin, Grigory Myasoedov, c. 1884-1886, oil on canvas; Tretyakov Gallery, Moscow","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMyasoyedov_by_Repin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Grigoriy_Grigoryevich_Myasoyedov_Rye.jpg/500px-Grigoriy_Grigoryevich_Myasoyedov_Rye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Grigoriy_Grigoryevich_Myasoyedov_Rye.jpg/1280px-Grigoriy_Grigoryevich_Myasoyedov_Rye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Grigoriy_Grigoryevich_Myasoyedov_Rye.jpg/500px-Grigoriy_Grigoryevich_Myasoyedov_Rye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Myasoedov, The Road in the Rye, 1881, oil on canvas; Tretyakov Gallery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrigoriy_Grigoryevich_Myasoyedov_Rye.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Harvest_time_%28Croppers%29_by_Grigory_Myasoedov_in_the_State_Russian_Museum_IMG_4818.jpg/500px-Harvest_time_%28Croppers%29_by_Grigory_Myasoedov_in_the_State_Russian_Museum_IMG_4818.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Harvest_time_%28Croppers%29_by_Grigory_Myasoedov_in_the_State_Russian_Museum_IMG_4818.jpg/1280px-Harvest_time_%28Croppers%29_by_Grigory_Myasoedov_in_the_State_Russian_Museum_IMG_4818.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Harvest_time_%28Croppers%29_by_Grigory_Myasoedov_in_the_State_Russian_Museum_IMG_4818.jpg/500px-Harvest_time_%28Croppers%29_by_Grigory_Myasoedov_in_the_State_Russian_Museum_IMG_4818.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The painting Harvest Time. Mowers in the State Museum of Fine Arts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarvest_time_(Croppers)_by_Grigory_Myasoedov_in_the_State_Russia